Preserve reset-after-FIN and reliable-reset validation on picoquic b4075dd.

RFC 9000 Section 3.1 permits a reset until all sent bytes and FIN are ACKed.
Use sent_offset, preserve context on refusal, and retain the provider's newer
misc-frame reset scheduling. A zero-length non-FIN ACK must record no range.
Reject a received Reliable Size exceeding Final Size, and let the common
stream-retirement check handle RESET_STREAM_AT ACKs on local UNI streams.
Retirement waits for both the reset ACK and all reliable-prefix byte ACKs,
including a stream whose FIN previously marked it closed.
Deliver arriving reliable-prefix bytes before signalling reset to the application.

The inclusive reliable-prefix boundary from the older 0005 patch is already
implemented upstream by picoquic_reliable_prefix_is_acked.
Tests: pq_reset_after_fin, constructed boundaries and simulated wire packets.

